{"aggregate_id": "01M55MX7JHMDN5W9QV66DESK4S", "aggregate_type": "Mission", "event_id": "01M55MX7PDBH18DWCYC9C0K56Z", "event_type": "MissionCreated", "payload": {"actor": "stijn@spec-kitty.ai", "created_at": "2026-10-17T19:20:06.076533+00:00", "friendly_name": "Built-in re-vendor: pin lockfile + vendor command + drift gate", "mission_id": "01M55MX7JHMDN5W9QV66DESK4S", "mission_number": null, "mission_slug": "builtin-revendor-pin-gate-01M55MX7", "mission_type": "software-dev", "purpose_context": "The committed packs/built-in tree can silently drift from its open-packs provenance source (as it just did: core moved 8 files past the recorded pin). ADR 2026-08-16-2 (amended 2026-10-11) keeps the tree committed and read-only, changed only via a pin bump, guarded by a drift gate. open-packs is now seeded+tagged (v0.1.0). Mission adds the core-side pin lockfile, the vendor command, the per-PR+release drift gate, and release re-verification, reusing landed primitives (core_compat, pack_clean_digest, regenerate-graph --pack-root). Out of scope: tree removal/materialization, packs/internal, the authoring flip.", "purpose_tldr": "Implement ADR 2026-08-16-2 Option B: pin the open-packs built-in source by commit SHA + digest, add a 'charter pack vendor' command, and a CI drift gate that keeps the committed packs/built-in tree provably equal to the pin (#3504).", "target_branch": "feat/builtin-revendor-pin-gate", "wp_count": 0}, "project_slug": "spec-kitty", "project_uuid": "8a4a7da6-a97c-4bb4-893a-b31664abfee4", "schema_version": "5.0.0", "timestamp": "2026-10-17T19:20:06.093070+00:00"}
